ogramming skills for a charitable foundation and got his dream job.\n  - John: John started playing board games, trying \"Dungeons of the Dragon.\" He enjoys electronic and rock music and used to play drums. He left his 3-year IT job for a new one aligned with his values.\n  - John: John plays drums, recently chatted with James about a new RPG with a cool story and tough gameplay, which sometimes causes lag and errors.\n  - computer game: James is developing a computer game based on childhood sketches, which contributes to his happiness alongside pets, travel, and pizza. John is passionate about the gaming industry and wants to organize state tournaments for games like CS:GO.\n  - game genres: John is trying new game genres, specifically strategy and RPG, instead of his usual shooters, due to encouragement from James; he plans to create competitions for them.\n  - John: John hosted a gaming tournament where he and his pals played Fortnite, Overwatch, and Apex Legends to raise money for a children's hospital.\n  - John: John started a startup making portable smokers, welding one prototype. He is launching a 2D adventure game soon and recently held a Fortnite gaming tourney to raise funds for a children's hospital.\n  - John: John collaborated with a game developer on an online board game and appreciates dogs for the joy and positivity they bring.\n  - John: John collaborated with a game developer to create a unique online board game and ended a conversation with James about it. Previously, he won a chess tournament and organized charity gaming tournaments.\n  - John: John is loving sharing his coding journey and tracking it. His favorite books are \"The Stormlight Archive\", \"Kingkiller Chronicle\", and he recommends \"The Expanse\" series for SF fans.\n  - game designs: John's siblings are coding while playing a simple, text-based adventure game. James asked John about new game designs.\n  - John: John is working on a cool coding project with his siblings, which is