nna contributed to a movie script. (event_time: 2022-10-23T00:00:00Z)\n  - The project Joanna finished is the screenplay (event_time: 2022-01-23T14:01:00Z)\n  - Joanna is the writer of the script that the actor liked. (event_time: 2022-11-11T00:06:00Z)\n  - Joanna worked hard on a script (event_time: 2022-11-09T17:54:00Z)\n  - Joanna's screenplay includes the genre drama. (event_time: 2022-01-23T14:01:00Z)\n</FACTS>\n\n# These are the most relevant entities\n# ENTITY_NAME: entity summary\n<ENTITIES>\n  - film festivals: Joanna submitted her screenplay to a film festival, feeling relief, excitement, and worry while hoping a producer or director selects it for the big screen.\n  - hope: Joanna experiences a tug-of-war of hope and doubt after wrapping up her second script, feeling a mix of relief and anxiety about future recognition.\n  - doubt: Joanna expressed a 'tug-of-war of hope and doubt' after finishing her second script, feeling a mix of excitement and terror about her work getting noticed.\n  - positive feedback: Joanna hopes finishing her first screenplay will lead to positive feedback and new opportunities.\n  - rejection letter: Joanna received a generic rejection letter without much feedback from a major company after finishing her screenplay, which made her feel bummed out and disheartened.\n  - seeing all of the characters and dialogue I wrote being acted out: Joanna experienced seeing all of the characters and dialogue she wrote being acted out, which was rewarding and the third time this has happened to her.\n  - new things: Joanna submitted a screenplay to a film contest and mentioned that people love it when she makes them new things.\n  - feelings: Writing is a way for Joanna to express her feelings, act as an escape, put thoughts down, and create something good from them, as words have a magical way of healing.\n  - script: Joanna is filming a movie from her road-trip script. An actor praised the script, making Joanna excited and giving her chills.\n  - writing projects: Joanna is busy with writing projects, which she finds to be the best thing ever, a mix of highs and lows. Writing is an escape, a way to express feelings, and healing.\n  - screenplay: Joanna wrote parts of a screenplay that appeared on the big screen yesterday and submitted a recent screenplay to a film contest.\n  - audition: Joanna had an audition for a writing gig yesterday; she feels mixed emotions but is excited, and Nate wished her luck.\n  - big screen: Joanna is writing a movie script, a love story with challenges, hoping to get it on the big screen.\n  - producer: Joanna hopes a producer or director will like her screenplay enough for it to be shown on the big screen.\n  - Joanna: Joanna is filming her own movie based on her road-trip script. She finds every day on set awesome and is excited to show her vision.\n  - romance: Joanna's first full screenplay, finished last Friday, is a mix of drama and romance.\n  - director: Joanna hopes a director falls in love with her screenplay to get it on the big screen.\n  - writing: Joanna feels she cannot stop writing recently, appreciating Nate's support and encouragement.\n  - directors: Joanna finished and printed her first full screenplay last Friday, hoping directors and producers will like it enough for it to be produced.\n  - road-trip script: Joanna is filming her own movie based on the road-trip script. She finds every day on set awesome and feels it is full of potential to show her vision.\n  - happiness: Joanna stated she will always remember moments that bring happiness and reminded Nate that it's important to stay happy and de-stress by doing what makes him happy.\n  - characters: Joanna saw characters she wrote acted out on the big screen for the third time, finding the experience rewarding. Nate inquired about the character on the left in a shared photo.\n  - writing gig: Joanna had an audition yesterday for a writing gig, feeling a mix of excitement and anxiety afterward. Nate previously encouraged her, noting her hard work and passion.\n  - feedback: Joanna received positive feedback that people are connecting with her writing, which Nate mentioned.\n  - romantic drama: Joanna mentioned a romantic drama about memory and relationships that she found to be very good.\n  - movie script: Joanna is filming a movie based on her road-trip script. She previously hoped for big-screen distribution, and Nate asked about future script submissions.\n  - Writing and creative projects: Joanna is busy with writing projects, which she finds to be a mix of highs and lows. Her journal is a major source of support for her writing endeavors.\n  - awesome characters: Joanna writes about \"wild worlds with awesome characters\" and is now in a writers group, feeling motivated by inspirational people.\n  - memory and relationships: Joanna mentioned a romantic drama about memory and relationships that she found to be very good.\n  - movie: Joanna is filming her movie based on her road-trip script. She finds every day on set awesome and enjoys showing her vision, with Nate asking about the coolest moment.\n</ENTITIES>\n","context_tokens":1981,"context_chars":8100,"retrieval_duration":0.18827557563781738,"response_duration":1.9984211921691895,"total_duration":2.186696767807007,"grade":true,"grade_reasoning":"The generated answer captures all the emotions mentioned in the gold answer, including relief, excitement, worry, and also adds hope and anxiety, which aligns with the overall sentiment.","completeness_grade":"COMPLETE","completeness_reasoning":"The context provides all the necessary emotions Joanna is feeling about her screenplay submission, including relief, excitement, worry, hope, and anxiety. Each of these emotions is explicitly mentioned in the facts, aligning perfectly with the golden answer. Therefore, the context is sufficient to fully answer the question.","missing_elements":[],"present_elements":["relief","excitement","worry","hope","anxiety"]},{"us