day. (event_time: 2022-04-16T00:00:00Z)\n  - Joanna has been working on something. (event_time: 2022-05-20T19:49:00Z)\n  - Joanna recently started writing a book. (event_time: 2022-07-10T14:34:00Z)\n  - A major company sent a rejection letter to Joanna after she finished her screenplay. (event_time: 2022-06-03T17:44:00Z)\n  - Joanna is currently working on a project that is both challenging and fulfilling (event_time: 2022-11-04T15:56:00Z)\n  - Nate thinks Joanna's accomplishment regarding her screenplay is amazing and encourages her to continue her pursuits. (event_time: 2022-01-23T14:01:00Z)\n  - Hiking has opened up a whole new world for Joanna. (event_time: 2022-05-12T15:35:00Z)\n  - The hard work and determination Joanna put into writing was rewarding (event_time: 2022-10-25T20:16:00Z)\n  - Nate congratulates Joanna on finishing something that required effort. (event_time: 2022-10-06T11:15:00Z)\n  - The rejection letter from the major company greatly disappointed Joanna. (event_time: 2022-06-03T17:44:00Z)\n  - Nate congratulates Joanna on her hard work paying off. (event_time: 2022-11-11T00:06:00Z)\n  - Joanna is currently doing okay. (event_time: 2022-09-05T18:03:00Z)\n  - Nate asks Joanna if something happened regarding the major company rejection. (event_time: 2022-06-03T17:44:00Z)\n  - Joanna possesses a lot of talent. (event_time: 2022-07-10T14:34:00Z)\n  - The project Joanna finished is the screenplay (event_time: 2022-01-23T14:01:00Z)\n  - Nate is proud of Joanna for exploring her personal experiences and feelings and staying strong and true to herself. (event_time: 2022-05-20T19:49:00Z)\n  - Nate asked Joanna what she has been up to. (event_time: 2022-05-02T11:54:00Z)\n  - Nate asked Joanna what she has been up to. (event_time: 2022-10-25T20:16:00Z)\n</FACTS>\n\n# These are the most relevant entities\n# ENTITY_NAME: entity summary\n<ENTITIES>\n  - page: Joanna described seeing characters she wrote jump off the page and become real on the big screen, which was the third time this has happened.\n  - major company: Joanna received a rejection letter from a major company after finishing her screenplay, which bummed her out. Nate asked if something specific happened with the company.\n  - the set: Joanna is filming her own movie on the set, which she describes as awesome and full of potential every day.\n  - Joanna: Joanna is filming her own movie based on her road-trip script. She finds every day on set awesome and is excited to show her vision.\n  - bookmark: Joanna finished a cute little bookmark for a lady at her writing club. Nate commented that the bookmark is great and she will love it.\n  - rejection letter: Joanna received a generic rejection letter without much feedback from a major company after finishing her screenplay, which made her feel bummed out and disheartened.\n  - writer: Joanna, identified as a writer, experienced a major setback when her laptop crashed, resulting in the loss of all her work.\n  - new trail: Joanna is hiking on a new trail with friends this weekend to see a waterfall.\n  - talent: Nate encouraged Joanna, affirming her incredible talent and promising her hard work will pay off. Joanna is using a road trip for research for her next movie.\n  - a person: Joanna experienced seeing characters and dialogue she wrote acted out, calling it an amazing and rewarding experience that was the third time this has happened.\n  - the last one: Joanna is inspired to write a story about a thirty-year-old woman on a self-discovery journey after a loss, similar to 'the last one'.\n  - creations: Joanna is proud of Nate's creations and complimented his gaming room. Nate is focusing on gaming and recently won a tournament.\n  - script: Joanna is filming a movie from her road-trip script. An actor praised the script, making Joanna excited and giving her chills.\n  - old notebooks: Joanna found old notebooks containing her early writings last week, showing her progress. Nate asked Joanna what she was working on in that notebook.\n  - sisterhood: Joanna watched a story exploring themes of sisterhood, love, and chasing dreams, which she recommended. She also finished writing her book last week after many late nights and edits.\n  - gorgeous sunset: Joanna took a picture of a gorgeous sunset while hiking near Fort Wayne last summer; Nate asked what inspired the photo.\n  - loss: Joanna received a rejection letter from a major company after finishing her screenplay, causing her to feel bummed out. The existing summary mentioned sadness and loss.\n  - success: Joanna congratulated Nate, describing an outcome as a huge success.\n  - passion: Joanna's writing is a huge part of her; Nate turned his passion for gaming into a career by winning an international tournament.\n  - picture: Nate complimented Joanna's drawings, asking what inspired them. Joanna previously mentioned seeing her writing acted out and Nate complimented a hiking picture.\n  - movies: Joanna highly rates movies (9-10/10) for emotional impact. Nate suggested watching one of Joanna's movies together.\n  - the trail: Joanna found an awesome, gorgeous hiking trail in her hometown. Nate is curious to see what the trail looks like and heard there is a nice trail just north of where he lives.\n  - Writing and creative projects: Joanna is busy with writing projects, which she finds to be a mix of highs and lows. Her journal is a major source of support for her writing endeavors.\n  - work: Joanna, a writer, lost all her work progress when her laptop crashed last week. Nate expressed sympathy and suggested backing up work in the future.\n  - third: Joanna asked Nate what made him get a 'third' after he mentioned not making it to the finals of a game tournament.\n  - favorite game: Joanna asked Nate what his favorite game is after he won a Valorant tournament.\n  - audience: Joanna advised Nate to watch other people's videos first to understand what his audience likes before posting his own.\n  - time off: Joanna mentioned that taking breaks and reducing stress is nice and asked Nate for movie recommendations.\n  - progress: Joanna is determined to keep grinding and moving ahead despite writing difficulties, after losing all her work progress when her laptop crashed. Nate expressed sympathy.\n  - goals: Joanna supports Nate in reaching his goals, and Nate will try again after not making the finals in his game tournament.\n</ENTITIES>\n","context_tokens":1976,"context_chars":7973,"retrieval_duration":0.19877123832702637,"response_duration":4.1724348068237305,"total_duration":4.371206045150757,"grade":true,"grade_reasoning":"The generated answer mentions that Joanna finished her screenplay in January 2022, which aligns with the gold answer's reference to her accomplishment.","completeness_grade":"COMPLETE","completeness_reasoning":"The context provides all necessary information to answer the question about Joanna's major achievement in January 2022. It explicitly states that Joanna finished working on her first full screenplay on January 21, 2022, which aligns perfectly with the golden answer that she finished her screenplay and printed it. There are no missing elements regarding this specific achievement.","missing_elements":[],"present_elements":["finished working on her first full screenplay (January 21, 2022)"]},{"user_id":null,"graph_id":"v2_full_onto_2_experiment_graph_8","test_id":"v2_full_onto_2_graph_8_qa_31","category":"3","difficulty":"unknown","query":"How might Evan and Sam's experiences with health and lifestyle changes influence their approach to stress and challenges?","golden_answer":"Their experiences likely lead them to view challenges as opportunities for growth and change. They both have embraced healthier lifestyles, indicating a proactive approach to managing stress and challenges.","hypothesis":"Evan and Sam's experiences with health and lifestyle changes significantly influence their approaches to stress and challenges. \n\nEvan has faced health challenges, including a recent health scare involving heart palpitations, which prompted him to focus on eating less processed food and sugary snacks. He acknowledges the importance of lifestyle changes and supports Sam in his health journey, emphasizing that small changes can lead to a healthier life. Evan also deals with personal challenges, such as the breakdown of his new Prius, which adds stress to his active lifestyle. However, he views this as an opportunity to explore new ways to stay active, indicating a proactive approach to managing stress.\n\nOn the other hand, Sam is dealing with work stress that contributes to unhealthy snacking and a lack of motivation. Despite feeling weighed down by health issues, he is motivated to make positive changes, such as adopting a healthier lifestyle and becoming a Weight Watchers coach. This role not only empowers him but also provides a sense of purpose in his quest for better health. Sam's efforts to manage his health and stress include planning outdoor activities, like hiking with Evan, which can serve as a positive outlet for stress relief.\n\nOverall, both Evan and Sam are navigating their health challenges by making lifestyle changes and supporting each other, which helps them cope with stress and setbacks more effectively. Their shared experiences foster a supportive environment that encourages resilience and proactive management of their health and stress.","context":"\nFACTS and ENTITIES represent relevant context to the current conversation.\n\n# These are the most relevant facts for the conversation along with the datetime of the event that the fact refers to.\n# If a fact mentions something happening a week ago, then the datetime will be the date time of last week and not the datetime\n# of when the fact was stated.\n# Timestamps in memories represent the actual time the event occurred, not the time the event was mentioned in a message.\n\n<FACTS>\n  - Evan is inquiring about how Sam's efforts in living healthier a