ee the dialogue she wrote acted out, noting it was the third time this happened. Seeing characters and dialogue from her writing performed was an amazing experience.\n  - Joanna: Joanna is filming her own movie based on her road-trip script. She finds every day on set awesome and is excited to show her vision.\n  - third: Joanna asked Nate what made him get a 'third' after he mentioned not making it to the finals of a game tournament.\n  - new opportunities: Joanna expressed hope that finishing her first screenplay would lead to new opportunities and positive feedback.\n  - book: Joanna finished writing and editing her book last week, exploring themes of sisterhood, love, and chasing dreams. The book had previously been shared with her writers group.\n  - movie script: Joanna is filming a movie based on her road-trip script. She previously hoped for big-screen distribution, and Nate asked about future script submissions.\n  - script: Joanna is filming a movie from her road-trip script. An actor praised the script, making Joanna excited and giving her chills.\n  - positive feedback: Joanna hopes finishing her first screenplay will lead to positive feedback and new opportunities.\n  - movie: Joanna is filming her movie based on her road-trip script. She finds every day on set awesome and enjoys showing her vision, with Nate asking about the coolest moment.\n  - passion: Joanna's writing is a huge part of her; Nate turned his passion for gaming into a career by winning an international tournament.\n  - director: Joanna hopes a director falls in love with her screenplay to get it on the big screen.\n  - Writing and creative projects: Joanna is busy with writing projects, which she finds to be a mix of highs and lows. Her journal is a major source of support for her writing endeavors.\n  - new things: Joanna submitted a screenplay to a film contest and mentioned that people love it when she makes them new things.\n  - writing projects: Joanna is busy with writing project