gs that bring you joy: Deborah advises Jolene to make time for 'things that bring you joy' to experience joy.\n  - partner de Jolene: Jolene and her partner planned to play console games together.\n  - Jolene's partner: Jolene's partner has values that encourage pursuing creative endeavors. They recently returned from a trip to Rio de Janeiro with Jolene, where they tried yoga classes.\n  - dogs: Deborah does not like dogs, which is why she has cats.\n  - love: Deborah connected love to her bond with her mother after hearing stories from her mom's friends; she also cited pets give priceless love and her cat Max needs love.\n  - someone close to Jolene: Someone close to Jolene used to bake cookies with her.\n  - daily routine: Jolene uses breathing, meditation, and yoga for challenges. Deborah meditates, does yoga, and teaches classes in the morning, jogs in a park, and spends evenings with loved ones.\n  - certain method: Deborah uses a \"certain method\" to help Jolene figure out what is important and urgent for better organization when overloaded.\n  - hobbies: Jolene is seeking tips for balancing hobbies and studies; Deborah focuses on teaching yoga and organizing a yoga event last month.\n  - Luna: Jolene inquired about Luna's age.\n  - fate: Jolene stated, \"I already know what fate awaits me if I do this!\"\n  - pets: Deborah stated that the love pets give is priceless. Previously, pets brought comfort, peace, and were great company.\n  - routines: Jolene is seeking new routines. Deborah suggested a gentle yoga flow focused on breathing and grounding to help Jolene cope, and offered to send a tutorial video.\n  - Something small: Jolene noted that something small can make a real difference and have a big impact.\n  - joy on the way: Jolene agreed to Deborah's advice to find joy on the way.\n  - setback with Jolene's project: Jolene experienced a huge setback with her project last week, causing her to lose all her work, which was frustrating and depressing. Deb