ived a generic rejection letter. (event_time: 2022-06-03T17:44:00Z)\n  - Joanna chose to write about connection because it is personal. (event_time: 2022-05-20T19:49:00Z)\n  - Joanna is concluding the conversation with someone. (event_time: 2022-10-06T11:15:00Z)\n  - Joanna perceives the rejection (presumably the rejection letter mentioned previously) as a step back sometimes. (event_time: 2022-06-03T17:44:00Z)\n  - Joanna wrote parts of a screenplay that were shown on the big screen the day before the current message. (event_time: 2022-06-04T00:00:00Z)\n  - Joanna chose to write about identity because it is personal. (event_time: 2022-05-20T19:49:00Z)\n  - Joanna currently excels in writing. (event_time: 2022-04-21T19:44:00Z)\n  - Joanna thanked someone for the recommendation. (event_time: 2022-08-22T10:57:00Z)\n  - The rejection letter from the major company greatly disappointed Joanna. (event_time: 2022-06-03T17:44:00Z)\n  - A major company sent a rejection letter to Joanna after she finished her screenplay. (event_time: 2022-06-03T17:44:00Z)\n  - Joanna's brother used to make cute notes for Joanna when they were kids. (event_time: 2022-11-07T20:10:00Z)\n  - The picture reminds Joanna of love. (event_time: 2022-06-05T14:12:00Z)\n</FACTS>\n\n# These are the most relevant entities\n# ENTITY_NAME: entity summary\n<ENTITIES>\n  - someone: Someone wrote Joanna a comforting letter last week after reading her blog post about a difficult moment, realizing her words had power.\n  - online blog post: Joanna wrote an online blog post about a hard moment in her life. Someone wrote Joanna a letter after reading it, saying her story brought them comfort.\n  - letter: Joanna received a letter last week from someone who read her online blog post about a hard moment; the writer felt comfort from her story. Nate commented that the letter is really awesome.\n  - a hard moment in my life: Joanna wrote an online blog post about 'a hard moment in my life'; someone later wrote her a letter saying the story brought them comfort.\n  - identity: Joanna is writing a personal story about loss, identity, and connection which she has had for ages but recently found the courage to write.\n  - childhood: Nate mentioned a letter that reminded Joanna of her childhood.\n  - writing: Joanna feels she cannot stop writing recently, appreciating Nate's support and encouragement.\n  - a person: Joanna experienced seeing characters and dialogue she wrote acted out, calling it an amazing and rewarding experience that was the third time this has happened.\n  - cute notes: Joanna's brother wrote the cute notes, which reminds her of sweet memories from when they were kids.\n  - love: Joanna mentioned themes of love, sisterhood, and chasing dreams explored well in a work she finished writing last week.\n  - loss: Joanna received a rejection letter from a major company after finishing her screenplay, causing her to feel bummed out. The existing summary mentioned sadness and loss.\n  - writing inspiration: Joanna uses taking breaks and self-care for writing inspiration to maintain inspiration and mental health, seeking balance.\n  - rejection letter: Joanna received a generic rejection letter without much feedback from a major company after finishing her screenplay, which made her feel bummed out and disheartened.\n  - the last one: Joanna is inspired to write a story about a thirty-year-old woman on a self-discovery journey after a loss, similar to 'the last one'.\n  - fond memories: Joanna encourages looking back on fond memories, stating it is such a blessing.\n  - comfort zone: Joanna commended Nate for stepping outside his comfort zone, calling it a great thing to do when helping strangers.\n  - drama: Joanna felt inspired to write a drama after hiking on amazing trails in her town.\n  - love story: Joanna is writing a movie script for a love story that involves many challenges; she is working hard and hopes to see it on the big screen.\n  - writers group: Joanna shared her book with her writers group last week and received great feedback. She recently finished a cute little bookmark for one of the ladies at her writing club.\n  - sisterhood: Joanna watched a story exploring themes of sisterhood, love, and chasing dreams, which she recommended. She also finished writing her book last week after many late nights and edits.\n  - passion: Joanna's writing is a huge part of her; Nate turned his passion for gaming into a career by winning an international tournament.\n  - work: Joanna, a writer, lost all her work progress when her laptop crashed last week. Nate expressed sympathy and suggested backing up work in the future.\n  - Writing and creative projects: Joanna is busy with writing projects, which she finds to be a mix of highs and lows. Her journal is a major source of support for her writing endeavors.\n  - moods: Joanna is finding comfort and creativity by tinkering with recipes when in certain moods, which Nate finds satisfying.\n  - journey: Joanna values the journey, appreciating happy moments to stay focused on dreams, and looks forward to showing it to Nate.\n  - writer: Joanna, identified as a writer, experienced a major setback when her laptop crashed, resulting in the loss of all her work.\n  - animals: Nate suggested Joanna write down things her animals like due to Joanna experiencing facial puffiness and itchiness around certain animals, causing avoidance.\n  - time off: Joanna mentioned that taking breaks and reducing stress is nice and asked Nate for movie recommendations.\n  - writing conventions: Joanna expressed interest in writing conventions after Nate mentioned attending a game convention, suggesting she might look into attending one.\n  - major company: Joanna received a rejection letter from a major company after finishing her screenplay, which bummed her out. Nate asked if something specific happened with the company.\n</ENTITIES>\n","context_tokens":1969,"context_chars":8092,"retrieval_duration":0.5214