o watch take shape, and she anticipates the final result.\n  - electrical engineering project: Jolene finished an electrical engineering project last week after a lot of work.\n  - milestone: Jolene finished a tough engineering project last month, calling it a big milestone she is proud of, having stuck it out despite problems. Deborah congratulated her.\n  - dreams: Jolene feels finishing a tough engineering project inspired her to keep striving for her dreams. Deborah recalls sharing dreams with her mom at a special place.\n  - Engineering assignments: Jolene is struggling to manage her Engineering assignments and is asking to discuss time management.\n  - engineer: Jolene, an engineer, is coping with an emotional rollercoaster but achieved a major milestone last week, causing relief and pride. She later asked Deborah for an explanation.\n  - engineering project: Jolene wants her engineering projects to use her talents to solve important problems, inspired by her mom stressing helping others. She focuses on new ideas and efficiency.\n  - work stress: Work stress is something that Jolene has been escaping for 3 years by playing a game.\n  - projects: Jolene is interested in projects that make a real difference, specifically sustainable initiatives and innovative environmental solutions, integrating values from loved ones.\n  - proyectos reales: Jolene aplicó lo aprendido en la escuela a proyectos reales, viendo sus ideas materializarse, lo cual es muy satisfactorio.\n  - engineering class: Jolene and her partner met in an engineering class in college, which blossomed into their relationship.\n  - engineering student: Jolene, an engineering student, wants to use her talents to do good, solve important problems, be innovative, and improve efficiency, influenced by her mother's value of helping others.\n  - Susie: Jolene mentioned that Susie is a great companion. Jolene has had Susie for two years.\n  - Neal Stephenson: Jolene read Neal Stephenson's book \"Avalanche\"