: Audrey finds cooking and eating food in the kitchen to be rewarding, therapeutic, and a form of self-care, often accompanied by music and wine.\n  - joyería: Audrey makes one-of-a-kind jewelry using recycled items like bottle caps and buttons, expressing creativity and sustainability while reducing waste.\n  - a glass of wine: Audrey pours a glass of wine while cooking and eating, describing it as therapeutic self-care.\n  - animal shelter: Audrey donates to an animal shelter as her way of helping out; Andrew's girlfriend volunteered at a pet shelter on Monday.\n  - fun: Audrey mentioned that self-care, including having fun, is important for managing stress and recommended Andrew do the same.\n  - collares: Audrey creates one-of-a-kind collares (necklaces) from recycled items like bottle caps and buttons, promoting creativity and sustainability while reducing waste.\n  - backyard: Audrey has a new, bigger backyard at her new place where she set up a doggy play area with agility equipment and toys for the pooches.\n  - this dish: Audrey finds cooking and eating 'this dish' rewarding, considering it self-care while listening to music and drinking wine.\n  - volunteer: A volunteer at the local pet store let Audrey meet their friendly and playful dog after Audrey saw a flyer for a positive reinforcement training class.\n  - gorgeous spot: Audrey inquired about the location of the \"gorgeous spot\" to take her dogs for a stroll.\n  - agility classes: Audrey started agility classes for her dogs at a dog park; she takes them twice a week for practice, which is a great physical, mental, and bonding workout.\n  - self-care activity: Audrey does at least one self-care activity daily, like treating herself, while Andrew incorporates coffee breaks and lunch walks for self-care.\n  - Audrey's pups: Audrey made an appointment with an animal behaviorist for her dogs due to abnormal behavior. She also joined a dog owners group to learn better care methods.\n  - Audrey's dogs: Aud