ate acquired a new family addition named Max and expressed pride in Joanna for staying strong and being true to herself.\n  - those things: Joanna expressed interest in doing 'those things' with Nate after Nate's game tournament was discussed.\n  - similar interests: Joanna and Nate established they have similar interests, leading Joanna to ask Nate about his preferred movie types.\n  - something sweet: Joanna expressed interest in trying Nate's sweet recipe, specifically noting she is always up for something sweet.\n  - movie reccomendations: Joanna is willing to give movie recommendations, which Nate usually likes more than random movie choices.\n  - the trail: Joanna found an awesome, gorgeous hiking trail in her hometown. Nate is curious to see what the trail looks like and heard there is a nice trail just north of where he lives.\n  - Chef: Joanna is referred to as a fellow Chef in the kitchen by Nate, and Joanna asks Nate for more tips on dairy-free baking.\n  - Jo: Joanna (Jo) asked Nate if he celebrated good feedback people are connecting with his writing. Previously, she asked about a couple he met while walking Max.\n  - random little things: Joanna gets super invested in 'random little things' and finds that having them makes life nicer.\n  - life: Joanna finds small things nice; Nate loves the rewarding feeling from winning a Valorant tournament and preparing for more.\n  - little things: Nate agreed that 'little things' like doggy playdates make life better.\n  - favorite game: Joanna asked Nate what his favorite game is after he won a Valorant tournament.\n  - Nate: Nate made homemade coconut ice cream with sprinkles. His game tournament was postponed, and he didn't make the finals. He creates YouTube gaming content. He expressed support for Joanna filming her movie.\n  - goals: Joanna supports Nate in reaching his goals, and Nate will try again after not making the finals in his game tournament.\n  - book recommendations: Nate is looking for book reco