 pride parade last Friday and was asked by Melanie about how she stays inclusive in her work.\n  - paintings: Caroline is preparing to show her paintings at an LGBTQ art show next month. She mentioned this when asking Melanie about creative outlets.\n  - poetry reading: Caroline attended a transgender poetry reading where transgender people shared stories; it was special, safe for self-expression, and empowering.\n  - Being ourselves: Caroline stated that 'Being ourselves' is a great feeling and an ongoing adventure of learning and growing.\n  - self-acceptance: Caroline stated that finding self-acceptance was a long process, but now she is ready to offer love and support, feeling empowered to make a positive difference.\n  - Melanie: Melanie congratulated Caroline on passing adoption agency interviews, viewing adoption as a loving way to build a family for needy kids, and encouraged Caroline to be herself.\n  - my own struggles: Caroline's past struggles made her feel alone, and sharing her story while volunteering at an LGBTQ+ youth center helped her support others.\n  - self-acceptance and love theme: Caroline loves the self-acceptance and love theme, which relates to her self-discovery journey; Melanie asked how art aids this process.\n  - who I really am: Caroline found out who she really is with invaluable help from friends, family, and mentors during tough times, and now wants to pass that support to others.\n  - self-discovery and acceptance journey: Melanie asked Caroline how art helps with her self-discovery and acceptance journey, in a conversation following Caroline's attendance at a pride parade.\n  - positive difference: Caroline is ready to offer love and support, aiming to make a positive difference in someone's life after achieving self-acceptance.\n  - dress: Melanie mentioned putting on a dress 5 years ago, in a message to Caroline.\n  - pottery: Melanie recently took a break from pottery due to an injury last month; Caroline offered support. Mela